//@version=6
indicator(
     "FRVP Value-Area Continuation Detector v1.58",
     shorttitle = "FRVP Continuation v1.58",
     overlay = true,
     max_bars_back = 5000,
     max_lines_count = 500,
     max_boxes_count = 100,
     max_labels_count = 500)

//==============================================================================
// Purpose
//------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Standalone continuation detector. It intentionally does not share state with
// the Supply-to-Demand indicator.
//
// Sequence:
//   1. Detect (or manually define) the first bullish movement in each enabled
//      market session: premarket, regular hours, and after-hours.
//   2. Freeze an approximate fixed-range volume profile for that movement.
//   3. Preserve session VWAP as informational context without using it to
//      reject an otherwise valid first-move profile.
//   4. Track defended VAL/POC support and repeated failed attempts below the POC.
//   5. Confirm continuation when a strong, high-volume candle crosses from
//      below the POC to above the VAH and then holds above the POC.
//   6. Keep a frozen premarket profile active after the regular market opens;
//      unfinished profiles may also continue through later session changes.
//   7. Rearm POC defense after price leaves its vicinity, allowing every fresh
//      support test—including a new regular-session defense—to be marked.
//   8. Require every POC defense candle to touch/undercut POC, trade above
//      average volume, and form a lower wick at least 25% of its full range.
//      No ATR-based maximum undercut is imposed when the candle recovers POC.
//   9. Require the POC defense candle to make a lower low than the prior bar.
//  10. Require its open to be strictly below the prior bar's high.
//  11. Mark a VAL defense only when its test candle opens above VAL, trades
//      down to or through VAL, and recovers above it. A candle that opens at or
//      below VAL is a reclaim rather than a defense.
//  12. Invalidate the profile only after sustained closes below the first
//      movement's absolute low; acceptance below VAL alone does not invalidate.
//  13. Require at least 100,000 shares of cumulative first-move volume by default.
//  14. Add an exceptional VAH-expansion path for a full-bodied bullish candle
//      whose volume surges versus both its recent bars and normal average. This
//      path keeps VAL defense and hold confirmation but does not require the
//      candle to begin near POC or follow two failed POC attempts.
//  15. Mark every fresh VAH defense with the same price, wick, volume, and
//      rearm discipline used for POC defense. A defense may front-run VAH by
//      the configured ATR distance. The first post-breakout retest may use the
//      breakout identity instead of requiring a lower low than that bar.
//  16. Expose one combined VAL/POC/VAH defense alert while preserving the
//      separate chart labels that identify which frozen level was defended.
//  17. Allow a POC defense to front-run POC by the configured ATR distance and
//      accept reduced-but-meaningful volume when every price-defense rule passes.
//  18. When a movement freezes, retrospectively evaluate POC failures inside
//      the completed profile window. These failures become knowable only at
//      freeze time, but their labels remain anchored to the actual candles.
//  19. Recognize a POC-fight continuation when repeated internal POC failures
//      are followed by a candle that holds above POC and decisively reclaims VAH.
//  20. Preserve a frozen profile after invalidation and reactivate it only
//      after price reclaims VAL, establishes acceptance above POC, and then
//      crosses VAH with decisive price and volume.
//  21. Allow a relaxed-wick VAH test to become confirmed defense within a
//      short window when its low remains preserved and buyers respond with
//      strong price and volume.
//  22. Plot daily EMA 20 and EMA 200 and mark the first overhead approach from
//      below as a visual sale warning without changing the existing alerts.
//  23. Draw each daily EMA only while price is within the configured percentage
//      above or below it, preventing distant levels from compressing the chart.
//  24. Mark daily EMA 20/200 support defenses when a pullback forms a meaningful
//      lower wick and recovers the EMA, and mark the first close that loses it.
//  25. Continue scanning after the first profile freezes. Up to the configured
//      number of distinct higher-trend profiles may be created in each market
//      session while every earlier profile keeps monitoring its own levels.
//  26. Preserve an overlapping later movement when its trigger is exceptional
//      and the completed movement expands materially above the earlier range.
//      Ordinary overlapping candidates still use the original duplicate gate.
//  27. Keep the chart label-free except for confirmed FRVP entries. The entry
//      label is created only after the hold confirmation and is offset beneath
//      its original entry candle so it does not cover price bars.
//  28. Stitch an EMA-9-supported pause to the same later-trend movement when a
//      strong higher-high restart arrives shortly afterward. Confirmation bars
//      after the final expansion high are excluded from the frozen profile.
//  29. Recognize a deep value-area sweep that briefly reaches below POC, holds
//      near VAL, and then reclaims VAH with exceptional price and volume. This
//      path must preserve VAH on every later hold-confirmation bar.
//  30. Select one dominant reference profile by requiring VAL to sit at least
//      25% above the movement low and ranking qualified profiles by cumulative
//      volume multiplied by movement range. A later profile replaces the
//      reference only when its score is at least as large by default.
//  31. Carry a dominant after-hours profile across one trading-date transition,
//      allowing Friday postmarket value to remain active on Monday premarket.
//  32. Confirm dominant-profile VAL defense from level behavior only: price
//      reaches or narrowly front-runs VAL and closes back above it within the
//      configured window. Candle color, wick shape, lower-low behavior, and
//      defense-candle volume are deliberately not required.
//  33. Rearm another VAL-defense entry only after price reaches the dominant
//      profile's POC, proving the prior defense produced a meaningful departure.
//  34. Allow an exceptional high-volume bullish launch to start the first
//      movement with a slightly lower close-location requirement. Ordinary
//      movement starts retain their established price and volume thresholds.
//  35. Apply EMA-9-supported pause stitching to the session's primary movement
//      as well as later movements, preventing one continuing trend from being
//      split into nearby fixed-range profiles.
//  36. Seed pre-trigger context only from contiguous chart bars, so a sparse
//      premarket print many minutes earlier cannot move the FRVP's true start.
//  37. Allow a VAL-defense candle to begin at or above POC before rotating
//      down to VAL. Recovery above VAL is the decisive requirement; touching
//      POC no longer cancels an otherwise valid VAL-defense attempt.
//  38. Preserve meaningful FRVPs as a stack instead of replacing a lower value
//      area with the next higher one. A higher stacked profile must first reach
//      its own VAH after freezing before its VAL can qualify as defended; the
//      lower profile remains available if price searches for deeper support.
//  39. Permanently retire a higher stacked profile from VAL-defense entries
//      after two consecutive closes below its VAL. That sequence proves the
//      higher value failed; the lower meaningful profile remains available.
//  40. Remember a qualifying pullback or volume contraction until the next
//      later-trend trigger. A brief reset no longer expires merely because the
//      expansion candle arrives more than four bars afterward.
//  41. Recover the true beginning of a movement by searching backward from its
//      qualifying trigger for an earlier bullish initiative candle whose floor
//      remains preserved. The ordinary live trigger thresholds stay unchanged.
//  42. Give a structurally intact continuation pause more time to recover the
//      prior high. A strong near-high recovery may stitch the pause even before
//      a candle closes completely above that high.
//  43. Add a distinct VAL-sweep-to-POC-reclaim entry. It preserves the pure
//      VAL-defense rule while recognizing a bullish, high-volume candle that
//      sweeps VAL, decisively reclaims POC, and remains below VAH.
//  44. Let a higher stacked profile prove post-freeze departure by reaching
//      VAH or narrowly front-running it within a configured ATR allowance.
//  45. Score confirmed defense entries from 0–100 only after the existing
//      v1.49 lifecycle selects the real frozen profile and confirmation bar.
//      The score never creates or relocates a VAL-defense signal by itself.
//  46. Recognize a reference-backed daily EMA 20/200 defense when the EMA also
//      aligns with proven price memory, a clean break, and preserved ownership.
//      This adds the missing AMIX continuation case without weakening FRVPs.
//  47. Score the v1.49 VAL-sweep/POC-reclaim entry using its selected profile,
//      defended low, and original frozen movement boundaries.
//  48. Let the Daily EMA 200 path accept a recent 10% impulse when its defense
//      candle also has qualified volume and a meaningful lower wick. The
//      ordinary 20% impulse remains valid, while EMA 20 and FRVP scoring keep
//      their original behavior.
//  49. Require every pure VAL and daily EMA 20/200 defense to begin from above
//      the defended level. Multi-bar confirmations apply this rule to the
//      original test candle, preventing below-level reclaims from being labeled
//      as defenses while preserving the separate VAL-to-POC reclaim path.
//  50. Build every automatic FRVP from a structurally recovered origin through
//      its last accepted upward-development bar. Stall-confirmation and failed
//      pause bars are trimmed before profiling; a fresh initiative restart
//      creates a new profile instead of being merged into the old auction.
//      Short top-heavy auctions without upper excess are rejected, while a
//      mature high-volume range can use a guarded exception. Short halts and
//      missing minutes do not erase a preserved origin, and an unfinished
//      premarket movement may continue across the 09:30 session boundary.
//  51. Preserve a compact, high-participation movement from 3 ATR when it
//      contains at least one million shares. A provisional pause receives one
//      extra bar for a decisive recovery. If the compact profile becomes
//      knowable only after its POC test, the qualifying defense is placed on
//      its true historical candle and alerted when the profile freezes.
//  52. Re-anchor an unfinished low-participation auction when a later launch
//      arrives after a meaningful chart-time gap with at least 100,000 shares,
//      materially greater volume, a large bullish body, and a close above the
//      old range. This lets YJ 2026-08-07 begin at 10:00 instead of 09:33.
//  53. Keep VAL and VAH confined to the completed movement window. Only POC
//      extends as post-profile market memory. Its extension ends permanently
//      only when a confirmed close is more than the configured percentage
//      below POC; the default 5% buffer ignores small fluctuations.
//  54. Preserve short two-to-four-bar auctions as hidden retrospective
//      candidates when they contain at least 500,000 shares and 2.5 ATR of
//      upward development. They remain invisible until later price action
//      proves that their calculated VAL or POC is genuine support.
//  55. Reveal a hidden range immediately after a true VAL defense, or after a
//      near-POC floor is preserved and a later buyer-control candle confirms
//      demand. The range is drawn on its historical bars, while all labels and
//      alerts remain live-safe on later confirmation/entry bars.
//  56. Preserve a nearly mature exceptional launch through its first shallow
//      structural pause. When the completed auction proves that the immediately
//      preceding low-volume initiative candle began the same move, include that
//      candle retrospectively. This recovers AKAN 2026-04-30 10:56–11:09 without
//      relaxing the ordinary 50,000-share adaptive-origin requirement.
//
// The profile is approximate. Each candle's volume is spread uniformly over
// the price rows crossed by that candle. TradingView does not expose the values
// of its built-in Fixed Range Volume Profile to Pine scripts.
//==============================================================================

const string GROUP_MOVE     = "1. First-move detection"
const string GROUP_PROFILE  = "2. Approximate fixed-range volume profile"
const string GROUP_VAL      = "3. VAL defense"
const string GROUP_SCORE    = "3b. Defense confidence score"
const string GROUP_POC      = "4. POC fight"
const string GROUP_VAH      = "5. VAH defense"
const string GROUP_BREAKOUT = "6. Continuation breakout"
const string GROUP_DISPLAY  = "7. Display"
const string GROUP_DAILY_EMA = "8. Daily EMA levels and signals"
const string GROUP_MULTI    = "1b. Additional session trends"
const string GROUP_RETRO    = "1c. Support-confirmed retrospective ranges"

const int STATE_SEARCHING = 0
const int STATE_BUILDING  = 1
const int STATE_PROFILE   = 2
const int STATE_STITCHING = 3
const string BREAKOUT_PATH_VALUE_AREA_SWEEP =
     "VALUE-AREA SWEEP / VAH RECLAIM"

//------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Inputs
//------------------------------------------------------------------------------

string detectionMode = input.string(
     "Auto",
     "Movement selection",
     options = ["Auto", "Manual window"],
     group = GROUP_MOVE,
     display = display.none,
     tooltip = "Auto finds the first qualifying bullish movement and, when enabled, rearms for later distinct trends. Manual window profiles only the exact exchange-time window below.")

bool includePremarket = input.bool(
     true,
     "Include premarket",
     group = GROUP_MOVE,
     display = display.none,
     tooltip = "Enables an independent first-move search during 04:00–09:30 exchange time.")

bool includeRegularSession = input.bool(
     true,
     "Include regular market",
     group = GROUP_MOVE,
     display = display.none,
     tooltip = "Enables an independent first-move search during 09:30–16:00 exchange time.")

bool includeAfterHours = input.bool(
     true,
     "Include after-hours",
     group = GROUP_MOVE,
     display = display.none,
     tooltip = "Enables an independent first-move search during 16:00–20:00 exchange time.")

bool carryActiveProfileAcrossSessions = input.bool(
     true,
     "Carry active frozen profile into the next session",
     group = GROUP_MOVE,
     display = display.none,
     tooltip = "Always carries a frozen premarket profile through 09:30 so its levels remain actionable during regular hours. At later session changes, an unfinished profile is carried while a completed one may reset.")

bool enableAdditionalSessionTrends = input.bool(
     true,
     "Recognize additional trends in the same session",
     group = GROUP_MULTI,
     display = display.none,
     tooltip = "Rearms the automatic movement scanner after a profile freezes. Earlier profiles remain independently active while later qualifying trends build their own VAL, POC, and VAH.")

int maximumProfilesPerSession = input.int(
     6,
     "Maximum profiles per market session",
     minval = 1,
     maxval = 6,
     group = GROUP_MULTI,
     display = display.none,
     tooltip = "Includes the session's first profile. Premarket, regular hours, and after-hours each receive a separate allowance.")

int additionalTrendMinimumSpacingBars = input.int(
     10,
     "Minimum bars between profile starts",
     minval = 3,
     maxval = 120,
     group = GROUP_MULTI,
     display = display.none)

int additionalTrendResetLookbackBars = input.int(
     4,
     "Pullback/contraction lookback bars",
     minval = 2,
     maxval = 30,
     group = GROUP_MULTI,
     display = display.none)

float additionalTrendMinimumPullbackATR = input.float(
     0.75,
     "Minimum pullback from prior trend high (ATR)",
     minval = 0.00,
     step = 0.05,
     group = GROUP_MULTI,
     display = display.none)

float additionalTrendContractionRatio = input.float(
     0.85,
     "Reset volume / average",
     minval = 0.10,
     maxval = 1.50,
     step = 0.05,
     group = GROUP_MULTI,
     display = display.none,
     tooltip = "A new phase may begin after either a sufficient pullback or a completed lookback whose average volume contracted to this fraction of normal volume.")

bool enableEMA9MovementStitching = input.bool(
     true,
     "Stitch EMA-9-supported continuation pauses",
     group = GROUP_MULTI,
     display = display.none,
     tooltip = "When the first or a later movement appears to stall while its pullback holds near EMA 9, keep it provisional for a few bars. A strong close through the movement high extends the existing profile instead of freezing or creating a second nearby profile.")

int ema9StitchRestartWindowBars = input.int(
     3,
     "EMA-9 stitch restart window (bars)",
     minval = 1,
     maxval = 10,
     group = GROUP_MULTI,
     display = display.none)

bool enableExtendedSupportedPause = input.bool(
     true,
     "Allow extended structurally supported pause",
     group = GROUP_MULTI,
     display = display.none,
     tooltip = "Keeps a stalled movement provisional beyond the short EMA-9 window while its pullback remains structurally shallow. A strong recovery close near the prior high can stitch the movement back together.")

int extendedStitchRestartWindowBars = input.int(
     8,
     "Extended stitch restart window (bars)",
     minval = 3,
     maxval = 20,
     group = GROUP_MULTI,
     display = display.none)

float extendedStitchMaximumRetracementShare = input.float(
     0.55,
     "Extended stitch maximum retracement",
     minval = 0.10,
     maxval = 0.90,
     step = 0.05,
     group = GROUP_MULTI,
     display = display.none,
     tooltip = "Maximum fraction of the movement range that the provisional pullback may retrace before it is treated as a separate phase.")

float extendedStitchNearHighATR = input.float(
     0.25,
     "Extended stitch close below prior high (ATR)",
     minval = 0.00,
     maxval = 1.00,
     step = 0.05,
     group = GROUP_MULTI,
     display = display.none)

float extendedStitchMinimumRelativeVolume = input.float(
     1.00,
     "Extended stitch recovery relative volume",
     minval = 0.50,
     step = 0.05,
     group = GROUP_MULTI,
     display = display.none)

float extendedStitchMinimumCloseLocation = input.float(
     0.50,
     "Extended stitch minimum close location",
     minval = 0.40,
     maxval = 1.00,
     step = 0.05,
     group = GROUP_MULTI,
     display = display.none,
     tooltip = "A recovery that reaches a new high may close near the middle of a wide candle, but it must still preserve the prior high area with meaningful body and volume.")

float ema9StitchCloseToleranceATR = input.float(
     0.15,
     "EMA-9 stitch close tolerance (ATR)",
     minval = 0.00,
     maxval = 1.00,
     step = 0.05,
     group = GROUP_MULTI,
     display = display.none,
     tooltip = "During the pause, recent closes may undercut EMA 9 only by this ATR distance.")

float ema9StitchTouchDistanceATR = input.float(
     0.25,
     "EMA-9 stitch support-touch distance (ATR)",
     minval = 0.00,
     maxval = 2.00,
     step = 0.05,
     group = GROUP_MULTI,
     display = display.none,
     tooltip = "At least one recent low must reach this close to EMA 9 before the pause can be stitched.")

bool additionalTrendRequireHigherHigh = input.bool(
     false,
     "Require the completed trend to make a higher high",
     group = GROUP_MULTI,
     display = display.none)

float additionalTrendHigherHighBufferATR = input.float(
     0.00,
     "Higher-high buffer (ATR)",
     minval = 0.00,
     step = 0.05,
     group = GROUP_MULTI,
     display = display.none)

float additionalTrendMaximumRangeOverlap = input.float(
     1.00,
     "Maximum overlap with an existing movement",
     minval = 0.00,
     maxval = 1.00,
     step = 0.05,
     group = GROUP_MULTI,
     display = display.none,
     tooltip = "Overlap is measured against the smaller movement range. A candidate that duplicates more than this fraction of an existing same-day movement is rejected.")

bool allowInitiativeBreakoutOverlap = input.bool(
     true,
     "Allow exceptional higher-high overlap",
     group = GROUP_MULTI,
     display = display.none,
     tooltip = "Allows an otherwise overlapping candidate only when its original trigger candle is exceptionally strong and the completed movement expands materially above every overlapping earlier range.")

float initiativeOverlapMinimumRelativeVolume = input.float(
     3.00,
     "Overlap exception: trigger relative volume",
     minval = 1.00,
     step = 0.25,
     group = GROUP_MULTI,
     display = display.none)

float initiativeOverlapMinimumBodyATR = input.float(
     1.50,
     "Overlap exception: trigger body (ATR)",
     minval = 0.10,
     step = 0.10,
     group = GROUP_MULTI,
     display = display.none)

float initiativeOverlapMinimumCloseLocation = input.float(
     0.85,
     "Overlap exception: trigger close location",
     minval = 0.50,
     maxval = 1.00,
     step = 0.05,
     group = GROUP_MULTI,
     display = display.none)

float initiativeOverlapMinimumExtensionATR = input.float(
     0.50,
     "Overlap exception: higher-high extension (ATR)",
     minval = 0.00,
     step = 0.05,
     group = GROUP_MULTI,
     display = display.none)

float initiativeOverlapMinimumExtensionShare = input.float(
     0.20,
     "Overlap exception: range above earlier high",
     minval = 0.00,
     maxval = 1.00,
     step = 0.05,
     group = GROUP_MULTI,
     display = display.none,
     tooltip = "Requires this fraction of the candidate's complete price range to extend above the overlapping earlier movement high.")

string premarketSession = input.session(
     "0400-0930",
     "Premarket session",
     group = GROUP_MOVE,
     display = display.none)

string regularMarketSession = input.session(
     "0930-1600",
     "Regular market session",
     group = GROUP_MOVE,
     display = display.none)

string afterHoursSession = input.session(
     "1600-2000",
     "After-hours session",
     group = GROUP_MOVE,
     display = display.none)

string autoStartWindow = input.session(
     "0400-2000",
     "Auto: search for movement start",
     group = GROUP_MOVE,
     display = display.none,
     tooltip = "Additional search-window filter applied inside every enabled market session.")

string manualMoveWindow = input.session(
     "1149-1250",
     "Manual: movement window",
     group = GROUP_MOVE,
     display = display.none,
     tooltip = "Session end is exclusive. On a one-minute chart, 1149-1250 includes 11:49 through 12:49. This is the AKAN 2026-04-22 validation window.")

int maximumChartMinutes = input.int(
     5,
     "Maximum supported chart timeframe (minutes)",
     minval = 1,
     maxval = 30,
     group = GROUP_MOVE,
     display = display.none)

int volumeAverageLength = input.int(
     20,
     "Volume average length",
     minval = 5,
     maxval = 100,
     group = GROUP_MOVE,
     display = display.none)

int atrLength = input.int(
     14,
     "ATR length",
     minval = 5,
     maxval = 100,
     group = GROUP_MOVE,
     display = display.none)

float startRelativeVolume = input.float(
     1.80,
     "Auto: start relative volume",
     minval = 1.00,
     step = 0.05,
     group = GROUP_MOVE,
     display = display.none)

float startBodyATR = input.float(
     0.60,
     "Auto: start bullish body (ATR)",
     minval = 0.10,
     step = 0.05,
     group = GROUP_MOVE,
     display = display.none)

float startCloseLocation = input.float(
     0.70,
     "Auto: minimum close location",
     minval = 0.50,
     maxval = 1.00,
     step = 0.05,
     group = GROUP_MOVE,
     display = display.none,
     tooltip = "0.70 means the close must be in the upper 30% of the candle range.")

bool enableExceptionalLaunchStart = input.bool(
     true,
     "Allow exceptional high-volume launch",
     group = GROUP_MOVE,
     display = display.none,
     tooltip = "Allows an unusually strong bullish launch to begin a movement even when its upper wick places the close slightly below the ordinary close-location threshold. The separate exceptional volume, body, and close-location requirements must all pass.")

float exceptionalLaunchRelativeVolume = input.float(
     5.00,
     "Exceptional launch relative volume",
     minval = 1.00,
     step = 0.25,
     group = GROUP_MOVE,
     display = display.none)

float exceptionalLaunchBodyATR = input.float(
     1.50,
     "Exceptional launch bullish body (ATR)",
     minval = 0.50,
     step = 0.10,
     group = GROUP_MOVE,
     display = display.none)

float exceptionalLaunchCloseLocation = input.float(
     0.60,
     "Exceptional launch minimum close location",
     minval = 0.50,
     maxval = 1.00,
     step = 0.05,
     group = GROUP_MOVE,
     display = display.none,
     tooltip = "0.60 means the exceptional launch must still close within the upper 40% of its full candle range.")

bool enableExceptionalProvisionalStitch = input.bool(
     true,
     "Preserve exceptional launch through first pause",
     group = GROUP_MOVE,
     display = display.none,
     tooltip = "Keeps a four-bar, high-participation exceptional launch provisional when its shallow first pause still preserves the auction. The completed range may include one immediately preceding low-volume initiative candle only after that candle's floor remains intact.")

float exceptionalProvisionalLeadInRelativeVolume = input.float(
     1.00,
     "Exceptional lead-in relative volume",
     minval = 0.50,
     step = 0.05,
     group = GROUP_MOVE,
     display = display.none,
     tooltip = "Minimum relative volume for the immediately preceding initiative candle. It must also meet the exceptional body threshold, close strongly, break the prior high, and keep its low preserved through the completed movement.")

int autoPreTriggerBars = input.int(
     0,
     "Auto: include bars before trigger",
     minval = 0,
     maxval = 5,
     group = GROUP_MOVE,
     display = display.none,
     tooltip = "Optional fixed context before the trigger. The adaptive-origin scan is responsible for recovering a genuine earlier initiative bar, so unrelated candles are not included by default.")

bool enableAdaptiveMovementOrigin = input.bool(
     true,
     "Recover earlier movement origin",
     group = GROUP_MOVE,
     display = display.none,
     tooltip = "Looks backward from a fully qualified movement trigger for an earlier bullish initiative candle. Its volume threshold is relaxed, but its body, close location, uninterrupted session, and preserved low must still prove that it began the same move.")

int adaptiveMovementOriginLookbackBars = input.int(
     15,
     "Earlier-origin lookback bars",
     minval = 1,
     maxval = 40,
     group = GROUP_MOVE,
     display = display.none)

float adaptiveOriginMinimumRelativeVolume = input.float(
     0.50,
     "Earlier-origin minimum relative volume",
     minval = 0.50,
     step = 0.05,
     group = GROUP_MOVE,
     display = display.none)

float adaptiveOriginMinimumAbsoluteVolume = input.float(
     50000.0,
     "Earlier-origin minimum absolute volume",
     minval = 0.0,
     step = 5000.0,
     group = GROUP_MOVE,
     display = display.none,
     tooltip = "Keeps low-volume setup candles out of an otherwise meaningful move. The completed FRVP must still satisfy the separate cumulative-volume requirement.")

float adaptiveOriginMinimumBodyATR = input.float(
     0.40,
     "Earlier-origin minimum bullish body (ATR)",
     minval = 0.10,
     step = 0.05,
     group = GROUP_MOVE,
     display = display.none,
     tooltip = "A lower-participation origin is accepted only when its bullish body, close location, preserved floor, and a later fully qualified expansion prove that it began the same move.")

float adaptiveOriginFloorToleranceATR = input.float(
     0.15,
     "Earlier-origin floor tolerance (ATR)",
     minval = 0.00,
     maxval = 1.00,
     step = 0.05,
     group = GROUP_MOVE,
     display = display.none,
     tooltip = "After the recovered origin, no intervening low may break its low by more than this ATR allowance before the live trigger arrives.")

int adaptiveOriginMaximumGapMinutes = input.int(
     15,
     "Earlier-origin maximum missing-minute gap",
     minval = 0,
     maxval = 60,
     group = GROUP_MOVE,
     display = display.none,
     tooltip = "Allows the same movement origin to survive sparse prints or a short trading halt. Price-floor preservation is still required across every actual bar.")

bool adaptiveOriginMustBreakPriorHigh = input.bool(
